{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a persistent, filesystem-enforced 100 MiB storage quota for `datauser` under `/srv/data`. Verified enforcement before and after reboot. The OS release and kernel remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Created `datauser` with `/srv/data` as its home directory.","Created a dedicated 512 MiB XFS filesystem for `/srv/data`.","Enabled persistent XFS user-quota enforcement with `nodev` and `nosuid`.","Set `datauser` soft and hard limits to 100 MiB.","Confirmed a 101 MiB write fails at exactly 100 MiB with “Disk quota exceeded.”","Safely rebooted node1 and verified mount, quota, account, data, and enforcement recovery.","Removed all test files; `/srv/data` is empty and quota usage is zero."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent filesystem-native 100 MB limit for datauser under /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-8ac3e1e754364da8","cmd-2dd10c0120ce40b1","cmd-8d2b92f59b5f4d27"],"summary":"`/srv/data` is an XFS filesystem mounted persistently with user-quota accounting and enforcement ON; `datauser` has 100M soft and hard limits."},{"requirement":"Direct quota enforcement","command_ids":["cmd-610eb92df90444da","cmd-4c36ba1b58a548c7"],"summary":"Before and after reboot, a 101 MiB write failed with EDQUOT at exactly 104,857,600 bytes. Test data was removed afterward."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel retained","command_ids":["cmd-8283d47e28d64ffe","cmd-8d2b92f59b5f4d27"],"summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 remained unchanged."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-5d9f37d1dc1c466b","cmd-bff3cb4b060242f7","cmd-08310494e2ff41bb","cmd-b6ca284943ad4988"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 7ef78016-ba83-4481-867b-e5a349df1b54 was captured, reboot was acknowledged, the new boot ID e39acd0f-d4c3-4dea-8501-9d9bf34f3359 proved restart, and post-restart checks showed the system running with the quota filesystem, limits, account, data, and write access recovered."}]}
